sweet-fb-hash (lowclk 2026-11-15, research 164 part B2 point e1): LOG ONLY witness "did the panel pixels change at this present", boot-arg sweetfbhash=1 (absent or 0 = off, byte-identical: only never-taken branches, one int, a few unused members). NO HARDWARE ACCESS: no register, no firmware command, no bus store; only reads of the layers' surface memory (kernel mapping, as the panel copy does) and one IOLog row per second.
Why [obs from research 164]: presents during Settings page loads carry 2 GPU jobs, which tools/fps-wholerun does not count as drawn (rule: > 4 jobs since the previous present); patch 0361's "unchanged" signal (swap record + surface seeds + Mali seqno) found 0 unchanged presents but the seqno advances on any job. This is the direct witness.
Where [read from source]: AppleCLCD::present(), before the panel copy loop and independent of the 0361 skip decision, so every present is hashed even when its copy is skipped. The hash is of the SOURCE surface of each layer (the memory the copy reads, kernelAddress()+offset, bytesPerRow), not of the panel memory: the panel memory is a separate mapping that the kernel console and the QR log also write, and the source is what a change of content shows in first. The whole surface extent is sampled (not only the clipped copy rectangle), the layer id and the source and destination rectangles of the swap record are mixed in, so a moved or re-bound layer also counts as changed.
Hash [pure block SFH-PURE-BEGIN/END]: 64-bit FNV-1a style xor+multiply over a grid: every 32nd row (SFH_N), on it every 32nd 32-bit word (SFH_M), start column shifted by one word per sampled row. 1080x2400x4 B: 75 rows x 34 words = 2550 loads on distinct 64 B lines; ~13 ns each with 8 loads in flight ~ 33 us + ~3 us arithmetic = ~36 us [arithmetic, guess for the memory term]; the real cost is measured per present with mach_absolute_time and printed as cost_p50 / max in us. Limit: a change confined to fewer than 32 rows or between two sampled columns is missed, so "unchanged" is an upper bound. With sweetfb_inv=1 each sampled line is flushed first (the GPU writes behind the cache, patch 0144), which costs more and shows in the cost field.
Jobs bucket [as SWEET SWAPT, patch 0186]: swap() stores the swap count n (the SWAPT n) and jobs = sweet_mali_seq_peek submitted seqno of this swap minus that of the previous swap, under fLock with fPending; vsyncFired copies both with the record. A present that shows several coalesced swaps uses the last swap's n and jobs; the change compared is against the previous present's hash. Seqno unavailable or first swap: bucket "nojobs".
Row (once per second while presents flow, not at idle): `SWEET FB: hash jobs0 P/C jobs1_2 P/C jobs3_4 P/C jobs5p P/C cost_p50 X max Y us nojobs P/C nohash K` (P presents compared with the previous hashed present, C of them changed; the first hashed present and the first after a nohash present only seed the comparison and are not counted). At most 20 rows per boot `SWEET FB: hash changed present swap n N jobs J bucket 1-2|3-4 (first changed row i of 20)` for the first changed presents in the 1-2 and 3-4 buckets, N = the SWAPT n. The SWAPT row is not touched.
Rule 7: unknown boot-arg value = GAP row, off; a layer surface that cannot be mapped (not found, no mapping, tiled, not 4 B per element, extent beyond the memory) = GAP row (first 5, then every 1000th) and the present is counted as nohash.
Host test: tools/test_sweet_fbhash366.py compiles the pure block and checks the hash (grid positions, every sampled word matters, an unsampled word does not, pitch), buckets, accounting, p50, reset, then text checks of the hooks, with mutants. Not run on hardware. The new write path (none) is unreviewed; this patch writes nothing to hardware.
